Scenario: A parent spawns a child before the selected environment is configured. The child sees it starting, waits, and receives the ready result after an ordinary parent turn-settings update.

## Window 1
-- request 1 (request; parent delegates while the environment is starting) --
00:message/developer[2]:
    [01] <PERMISSIONS_INSTRUCTIONS>
    [02] <ENVIRONMENTS_INSTRUCTIONS>
01:message/developer:
    You are `/root`. Own the result and coordinate delegated work. Agent messages arrive in analysis. `send_...thout starting a turn. `followup_task` starts a turn. [hash=57c7402ce89cae25]
    Call collaboration tools directly, not inside `functions.exec`. Agents share the filesystem and working ...ctory. Coordinate edits and preserve others' changes. [hash=65cb900ff14c98ef]
    Prefer waits of minutes with `wait_agent` to busy polling.

    At most 4 agents may be active, including you.

    Set `model` or `reasoning_effort` only when explicitly requested by the user, AGENTS.md, or skills. Over...ed or `"all"` inherits the parent's model and effort. [hash=75b60222a0f8595a]
02:message/developer:
    <multi_agent_mode>This replaces proactive-delegation guidance. Spawn agents only when explicitly request...e AGENTS.md or skill instructions.</multi_agent_mode> [hash=72a2fd98b66d3a10]
